<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry VII, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1275–<a href="/years/1313">1313</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Henry of Luxembourg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry VII was count of Luxembourg, elected king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1308 and crowned emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1312, the first since Frederick II. On his Italian expedition of 1310–1313 he tried to restore imperial authority, naming imperial vicars such as the Pico at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirandola">Mirandola</a> and besieging rebellious <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brescia</a> in 1311. He died near Siena in 1313. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-bohemia">John the Blind</a> became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, founding Luxembourg power there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-vii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Henry VII, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="560" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tino_di_camaino,_elementi_dal_monumento_funebre_di_arrigo_VII,_1315,_09_l%27imperatore_in_trono_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
